WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.270
Ask an accountant and an economist
about the same small business.

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.420
You can get two different answers.

3
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.150
A coffee shop brings in
120,000 dollars a year

4
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.280
and pays out 85,000 in bills.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.820
The accountant sees
35,000 dollars of profit.

6
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.240
The economist sees zero.

7
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.500
Both have done the math correctly.

8
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.870
So why might a business
that brings in money

9
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.470
every year still be making no real profit?

10
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.880
In this mission, you'll rebuild the
shop's year the way an economist does.

11
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.370
Then you'll move a firm's price and
watch its profit rectangle grow,

12
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.010
vanish and turn into a loss.

13
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.890
Your mission: find out what the economist
counts that the accountant leaves out.
